  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton obligated $1.8B in FY2026 to date across 278 awards, with an average award size of $6.4M. Peraton obligations are down 15.5% year over year. Peraton saw a multi-year climb from $466M in FY21 to $2.1B in FY25 before the FY26 partial total of $1.8B. Peraton receives the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations from the General Services Administration, followed by the Department of Defense and the Department of Transportation. Peraton work is concentrated in Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services, which together account for more than half of FY2026 to date obligations. Peraton also records significant activity in Custom Computer Programming Services and Other Computer Related Services. Peraton engagements span civilian and defense buyers, with notable amounts from NASA, HHS, and the Department of State. Peraton award counts and average award size indicate a mix of small and large task orders rather than a single large contract driving the total. Peraton year-to-date totals are partial for the fiscal year and reflect obligations rather than full contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Peraton's biggest agency customers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "General Services Administration obligated $644M with Peraton in FY2026 to date. Department of Defense obligated $370M and the Department of Transportation obligated $213M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $186M, and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $115M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and services drive Peraton's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Peraton at $855M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services contributed $392M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $153M and Other Computer Related Services at $124M. Telecommunications, computing infrastructure, and specialized services such as Landscape Architectural Services and Research and Development in Nanotechnology appear in the top markets."
      }
    ]
  },
